{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 proof that for finitely supported couplings (X, Y) with E[Y | X] = X and mu(Y) = E[X | Y], a convex (or continuous) f : R -> R satisfies E[f(X) - f(mu(Y))] <= E[f(Y) - f(X)] for every coupling iff f is a quadratic a t^2 + b t + c with a >= 0 (Theorem 1); the same characterisation holds for the smaller class Y = X + Z with Z independent of X and E Z = 0 (Theorem 2); and x^4, which is convex with convex second derivative, is a counterexample to the conjecture of the asker of MathOverflow question 451543.",
